; dsv4-control-leakfree-band.fk — does the native centroid adapter GENERALIZE, leakage-free?
;
; The shipped report gives 142/150 held-out but leakage=150 (every held-out template is memorized),
; so it names its own verdict "insufficient-template-leakage" and refuses. This band drives the
; leak-free FAMILY split (dsv4-control-leakfree.fk): train and held-out share vocabulary but no
; sanitized template, so a correct held-out prediction is a genuine unseen COMBINATION.
;
; PREDICTIONS, written before the run:
;   leakage           = 0        (families disjoint by construction)
;   held-out total    = 120      (12 families x 2 x 5 classes)
;   train total       = 480
;   distinct held-out = 12       (WRONG — corrected to 60, see below)
;   baseline          = 24       (balanced -> majority class = 20%)
;   diagonal          > 24       (the claim under test: does it beat the baseline?)
;
; The distinct-template prediction was wrong and the run corrected it: the sanitized template is
; context + " " + STATE, and the state TEXT is class-dependent. So one held-out FAMILY (a fixed
; (context-index, state-index) pair) yields five DIFFERENT sanitized strings, one per class. The
; structural invariant is therefore 12 families x 5 classes = 60 distinct held-out templates, not
; 12. That does not touch leakage (still 0 — train/held families are disjoint within every class).
;
; Verdict 7 when the frontier's core claim lands:
;   1  leakage == 0                          — the split is genuinely leak-free
;   2  diagonal > baseline                   — the trained weight beats predict-the-majority
;   4  split is a clean partition            — distinct-held==60, train==480, held==120
;
; PROOF LEVEL: pure Form (no GPU, no floats past the centroid ints). Runs on any arm via fkwu --src.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/dsv4-control-leakfree.fk

(do
    (let r (dclf-report))
    (let diagonal (nth r 1))
    (let leakage  (nth r 2))
    (let total    (nth r 3))
    (let baseline (nth r 4))
    (let distinct (nth r 5))
    (let train-n  (nth r 6))
    (let held-n   (nth r 7))

    (print (str_concat "held-out correct (diagonal) = " (int_to_str diagonal)))
    (print (str_concat "held-out total              = " (int_to_str total)))
    (print (str_concat "baseline (majority class)   = " (int_to_str baseline)))
    (print (str_concat "leakage                     = " (int_to_str leakage)))
    (print (str_concat "distinct held-out templates = " (int_to_str distinct)))
    (print (str_concat "train rows                  = " (int_to_str train-n)))
    (print (str_concat "held-out rows               = " (int_to_str held-n)))

    (let b1 (if (eq leakage 0) 1 0))
    (let b2 (if (gt diagonal baseline) 1 0))
    (let b4 (if (eq distinct 60) (if (eq train-n 480) (if (eq held-n 120) 1 0) 0) 0))
    (print (str_concat "bit1 leakage==0        = " (int_to_str b1)))
    (print (str_concat "bit2 diagonal>baseline = " (int_to_str b2)))
    (print (str_concat "bit4 clean partition   = " (int_to_str b4)))
    (let verdict (add b1 (add (mul 2 b2) (mul 4 b4))))
    (print (str_concat "Verdict: " (int_to_str verdict)))
    verdict)
